# Knowledge Base Maintenance

The `knowledge/` folder is the system of record for this codebase. It lives
alongside [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) at the repository root.

> Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and
> [`knowledge/product-specs/index.md`](../../knowledge/product-specs/index.md)
> at the start of any non-trivial task. The agent that comes after you
> will thank you.

## When to update

Update the knowledge base when you:

1. **Add a new user-visible feature** → create a spec in
   `knowledge/product-specs/<slug>.md` using
   [`knowledge/templates/product-spec.template.md`](../../knowledge/templates/product-spec.template.md)
   and add it to [`knowledge/product-specs/index.md`](../../knowledge/product-specs/index.md).
   **This is mandatory.**
2. **Change an existing feature's data model, API shape, agent tool
   surface, or AI prompt** → edit its spec.
3. **Add or change a Prisma model** → if the change is non-trivial,
   document it in the relevant spec; the migration itself is the source
   of truth.
4. **Introduce an architectural pattern worth preserving** → add a design
   doc at `knowledge/design-docs/<slug>.md` and list it in
   [`knowledge/design-docs/index.md`](../../knowledge/design-docs/index.md).
5. **Change `.cursor/skills/` or `.cursor/rules/`** → cross-link the
   relevant spec to the updated skill or rule.
6. **Ship something user-visible** → also add a CHANGELOG entry to
   [`src/lib/marketing-content.ts`](../../src/lib/marketing-content.ts).
   See [`changelog`](changelog.mdc).

## Specs are not marketing copy

Specs describe what a feature does and how to change it safely. Marketing
language (claims, benefits, taglines) belongs in
[`src/lib/marketing-content.ts`](../../src/lib/marketing-content.ts).
Never duplicate.

## Plans for non-trivial work

- Active multi-step plans: drop a markdown file in
  [`knowledge/exec-plans/active/`](../../knowledge/exec-plans/active).
- When the plan ships: move the file to `completed/`. Don't delete it —
  the next agent learns from how the previous one approached the work.

## When in doubt

Link instead of inlining. The knowledge base works because it's a graph,
not a single document.
